  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:sphmc-smoothed-hessian-bounds",
    "anchor": "SPHMC arXiv:2609.06906v1 Sections1-3 standing beta=1/alpha=kappa^-1/RGO/smoothing and Section4.1 S4.E1, Lemma4.1 S4.Thmtheorem1, S4.Ex4-6; actual unreflected posterior covariance and source unnormalized V_eta. Primary-first Smoothed_Hessian_lower_source_preread.md.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Thmtheorem1",
    "original_text": "Exact independently sealed bounded statement:\nSource C2 V with beta=1 and alpha=kappa^-1; kappa>=1; actual allpoint/allvector curvature kappa^-1*norma^2<=D2V[a,a]<=norma^2; source0<eta<=1 retained.\nActual source UNNORMALIZED exp(-V_eta)=exp(-V)*Gaussian_eta, normalized Gibbs mu=volume.tilted(-V), unreflected R_y=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)). Finite Hilbert/Borel including0 is disclosed representation extension.\nNo partition, covariance, moment, derivative or PI certificate on this source theorem. Actual probability, posterior vectorL2, C2, U=V_eta+logZV, both true Hessian bounds and global Lipschitz are produced internally. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher derivative, numerical kernel, cost or main claim.\nFor the actual source Gaussian-smoothed unnormalized potential and true RGO posterior, produce probability and vectorL2, covariance upper norma^2/(kappa^-1+eta^-1), C2 regularity and (kappa+eta)^-1*norma^2<=D2V_eta(y)[a,a]<=(1+eta)^-1*norma^2, and true1-Lipschitz gradient. This is the analytic Lemma4.1, not an algorithm/main theorem.\nCanonical BOTH-curvature Gibbs linear covariance upper with genuine vectorL2, actual positive partition and probability normalization; not full anisotropic Brascamp-Lieb. Actual source beta=1 alpha=kappa^-1, 1<=kappa, 0<eta<=1; genuine posterior law R_y, internally produced probability/vectorL2/positive partitions/C2 and normalized-U versus unnormalized-V_eta constant shift. Derive true covariance upper and both Hessian bounds (kappa+eta)^-1 and (1+eta)^-1, then true 1-Lipschitz gradient. Finite real Hilbert/Borel including zero dimension is disclosed representation extension. No input covariance/PI/oracle/moment/normalizer certificate on source Anchor. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher smoothing derivatives, algorithm/Wp/proxy-warmness/main/querycost/composition. PBPS reflected quarter law and source-score remain separate. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
    "text_sha256": "161d55c46dfc272ccbe91a3875736118dc3cda0cf60b6078c1e2d74dc37982cc"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.SmoothedHessianBounds.smoothed_hessian_bounds",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/SmoothedHessianBounds.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [CompleteSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {κ η : ℝ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x a : E, κ⁻¹*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x a a ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x a a ≤ ‖a‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hη1 : η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let C := ((Real.sqrt (2*Real.pi*η))⁻¹)^Module.finrank ℝ E\n    let A := fun y : E => C*∫ x, Real.exp (-V x-‖y-x‖^2/(2*η)) ∂(volume : Measure E)\n    let Vη := fun y => -Real.log (A y)\n    let R := fun y : E => μ.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y‖^2/(2*η))\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 Vη ∧\n      (∀ y, IsProbabilityMeasure (R y) ∧ MemLp id 2 (R y) ∧\n        (∀ a, ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin (R y) a a ≤ ‖a‖^2/(κ⁻¹+η⁻¹)) ∧\n        ∀ a, (1/(κ+η))*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ Vη) y a a ∧\n          fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ Vη) y a a ≤ (1/(1+η))*‖a‖^2) ∧\n      LipschitzWith (1 : ℝ≥0) (gradient Vη)",
    "statement_sha256": "2231be45294441c4f0be3b703665e36b5bfddb9d13a7f92dbb41fd89a4603df6",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "Measure.tilted mu f = mu.withDensity (fun x => ENNReal.ofReal(exp(f x)/(integral exp(f) dmu))); normalization is totalized if exponential integrability fails. IsProbabilityMeasure nu means nu(univ)=1.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin mu = ContinuousLinearMap.bilinearComp (covarianceBilinDual mu) (toDualMap R E).toContinuousLinearMap (toDualMap R E).toContinuousLinearMap. With genuine MemLp id2mu and finite probability it equals integral inner(a,x-meanX)*inner(b,x-meanX)dmu. Outside vectorL2 the covariance bilinear is zero, not a covariance estimate.",
      "MemLp id2nu denotes genuine AE strong measurability and finite L2 norm of the position vector. ContDiff R2 denotes actual twice continuously differentiable function, fderiv is genuine Frechet derivative.",
      "gradient f x = (InnerProductSpace.toDual R E).symm(fderiv R f x); true Riesz gradient in the given real Hilbert metric. LipschitzWith1 gradient is the actual global metric inequality.",
      "The conclusion potentials/laws are literal let bodies in the signatures. Finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel carrier includes zero dimension, no Nontrivial premise. No nested project-owned estimate-certificate aliases occur in either signature."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Focused3877/standard3; independent statement/source-topology accepted before proof search. Wholemath/blind/source/exact/integration/exposition pending."
  },
  "source_review": {
    "state": "accepted",
    "reviewer": "phase_source_reviewer_20261005",
    "independent_from_formalizer": true,
    "independent_from_decoder": true,
    "evidence": "Fresh primary v1 Section1/2/3.1/4.1 read before current candidate/reconstruction; independent original scoped contract cbc5a6a73e61ed04f89e4e23e47df56428a9810f45f06ca295b7cd53d9d9d0fd. Entire both production modules,113Test and13readersteps/APIs inspected; exact sealed signatures, primary semantics and both separate decoder reconstructions compared in all seven slots. Genuine variance/moments, literal law/normalization/U shift, exact Hessian constants and1Lipschitz verified by proof inspection, not inferred from green Lean or mathematical reviewer. Four truthful provenance metadata repairs plus decoder-only two audit bindings independently reconciled; all current raw/LF inputs frozen. No full anisotropicBL, higher regularity or sampler/main/cost/composition credit.",
    "review_run_sha256": "de06492203272ac3eb7f774ab62f2ea345f7ec98cd5a381b073b0fd3d3115e6a",
